   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there,<div><br></div><div>If you find yourself assigning an output (in this case, &quot;output$map &lt;- renderPlot(...)&quot;) inside of an observe, that&#39;s usually a good indication that you&#39;ve gone astray. (The same goes for creating an observer inside of an output&#39;s renderPlot function.)</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>When you assign output$map &lt;- renderPlot(...), that&#39;s not saying &quot;Update the output &#39;map&#39; with this logic, right now.&quot; Instead it&#39;s saying, &quot;The output &#39;map&#39; should always reflect this logic; make sure it stays up-to-date.&quot; So in this case you probably want something like this:</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>s_options &lt;- buildOptions()</div><div><br></div><div>shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>  updateSelectInput(session,&quot;ONE&quot;, choices = s_options)</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n\r\n  output$map &lt;- renderPlot({<br></div><div>    firstChoice &lt;- input$ONE</div><div>    secondChoice &lt;- input$TWO</div><div>    if (is.null(input$TWO))  # or maybe this should be a check for &quot;&quot;, not sure</div>\r\n\r\n<div>      return(NULL)</div><div>    otherValue &lt;- doSomething(input$ONE, input$TWO)<br></div><div>    plotSomething(otherValue)</div><div>  })</div><div><br></div><div>  # The only reason we need an observe is to update the choices for TWO.</div>\r\n\r\n<div>  observe({<br></div><div>    updateSelectInput(session, &quot;TWO&quot;,</div><div>      choices = getChoicesForTwo(input$ONE))</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div>Note that you don&#39;t need to tell Shiny when output$map needs to be updated. It automatically infers that output$map depends on input$ONE and input$TWO, so whenever either of those changes it will automatically re-execute.</div>\r\n\r\n</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
