     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Tuesday, December 3, 2013 4:47:25 PM UTC-2, Joe Cheng [RStudio] wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there,<div><br></div><div>If you find yourself assigning an output (in this case, &quot;output$map &lt;- renderPlot(...)&quot;) inside of an observe, that&#39;s usually a good indication that you&#39;ve gone astray. (The same goes for creating an observer inside of an output&#39;s renderPlot function.)</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>When you assign output$map &lt;- renderPlot(...), that&#39;s not saying &quot;Update the output &#39;map&#39; with this logic, right now.&quot; Instead it&#39;s saying, &quot;The output &#39;map&#39; should always reflect this logic; make sure it stays up-to-date.&quot; So in this case you probably want something like this:</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>s_options &lt;- buildOptions()</div><div><br></div><div>shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {</div><div>  updateSelectInput(session,&quot;ONE&quot;, choices = s_options)</div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n  output$map &lt;- renderPlot({<br></div><div>    firstChoice &lt;- input$ONE</div><div>    secondChoice &lt;- input$TWO</div><div>    if (is.null(input$TWO))  # or maybe this should be a check for &quot;&quot;, not sure</div>\r\n\r\n<div>      return(NULL)</div><div>    otherValue &lt;- doSomething(input$ONE, input$TWO)<br></div><div>    plotSomething(otherValue)</div><div>  })</div><div><br></div><div>  # The only reason we need an observe is to update the choices for TWO.</div>\r\n\r\n<div>  observe({<br></div><div>    updateSelectInput(session, &quot;TWO&quot;,</div><div>      choices = getChoicesForTwo(input$ONE))</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div>Note that you don&#39;t need to tell Shiny when output$map needs to be updated. It automatically infers that output$map depends on input$ONE and input$TWO, so whenever either of those changes it will automatically re-execute.</div>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Dec 3, 2013 at 1:33 AM, João Carlos <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">jcani...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>Hello,</div><div><br></div><div>I need help because I still struggle with the concepts of reactive components.</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>I have 2 selectInput whose values are related. I managed to make it work. Selections made on the first change the options in the first second. The options for the first are built from values read from a file and never change.</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>The problem is that after making a selection in the second control ( ONE &gt;&gt;&gt; TWO )  I need to select some option 2 times in the first control so it responds again.</div><div><br></div><div>However if I make selections only the first or only the second all the functions respond correctly.</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Below is a simplified version of what I&#39;m doing.</div><div><br></div><div>Where am I going wrong?</div><div><br></div><div>Thankful in advance.</div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">s_options &lt;- buildOptions()</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n<br></blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">shinyServer( function(input, output, session) </blockquote>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">{</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n  updateSelectInput(session,&quot;ONE&quot;, choices = s_options)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n  </blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">  observe(</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n    {</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">    </blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n    firstChoice &lt;- input$ONE</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">    </blockquote>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">    otherValue &lt;-  doSomething(firstChoice)</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">    </blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n    output$map &lt;- renderPlot({ plotSomething(otherValue)})</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n      </blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">    })</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n     </blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">  observe(</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n    {</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">      secondChoice = input$TWO</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">      </blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n      otherValue &lt;-  doSomething(firstChoice)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n      </blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">      output$map &lt;- renderPlot({ plotSomething(otherValue) })</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">    })</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n    </blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">})</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n   </blockquote></blockquote></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405845825000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0iTfocHyVNtwKijbvAgRgd\">https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n</blockquote></div></div>"
